e same rule without a permit.\n\nRule: core.git:checkout-discard\n\nIf this operation is truly needed, ask the user for explicit permission and have them run the command manually.","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MReg6ypS7c2fQuwvSgxFes"}]},"uuid":"859702b1-97ae-46db-9f4e-cbae479af019","timestamp":"2026-10-05T12:46:59.710Z","toolUseResult":"Error: PreToolUse:Bash hook error: BLOCKED by dcg\n\nTip: dcg explain \"cd ~/.claude && S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/67004755-6eb9-4324-a41f-97820a746f73/scratchpad; git diff settings.json > $S/settings-dcg-dup.patch && cp $S/settings-dcg-dup.patch ~/.claude/scripts/logs/settings-dcg-dup-2026-10-05.patch 2>/dev/null; git checkout -- settings.json && git add -A && git commit -qm \\\"mac snapshot before sync\\\" && git pull --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -3 && git push -q 2>&1 | tail -3; git log --oneline -1\nfor r in skills global-memory; do echo \\\"== $r\\\"; cd ~/.claude/$r; git add -A; git diff --cached --quiet || git commit -qm \\\"mac snapshot before sync\\\"; B=$(git rev-parse HEAD); git pull --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -3; echo \\\"new commits: $(git rev-list --count $B..HEAD)\\\"; git log --oneline -1; git push -q 2>&1 | tail -3; done\"\n\nReason: git checkout -- discards uncommitted changes permanently. Use 'git stash' first.\n\nExplanation: git checkout -- <path> discards all uncommitted changes to the specified files in your working directory. These changes are permanently lost - they cannot be recovered because they were never committed.\n             \n             Safer alternatives:\n             - git stash: Save changes temporarily, restore later with 'git stash pop'\n             - git diff <path>: Review what would be lost before discarding\n             \n             Preview changes first:\n               git diff -- <path>\n             \n             Recovering from a failed `git pull --rebase`?\n             Run `dcg rebase-recover` in this repo, then retry the command. This issues a short-live