/ archive); weekly-review Step 4b (claude-skills `8210e09`). Header: N paused rows awaiting a decision (85 today).\n  9. `render.py`, `dashboard.html`, `pulse.md` retired; Artifact frozen with a banner (v24); `/project` skill (claude-skills `e23aa73`), KeystoneOS morning-cadence (`cf08abe`), DEV router (`9c5303e`). The snapshot's Front Burner section (fed by pulse.md) is gone on purpose. Command centre never had a projects tab: nothing to remove.\n  - Also: `save_registry` retries `os.replace` on WinError 5 (a reader holding the file); that was the flaky undo tests.\n- 2026-10-03 (evening): **PM system merged** (PR #2, `5ba7647`) and smoke-tested from master: `board.py --background` starts then reuses; `sweep` lists 10 of 85. Restyle pass (neutral greys, system font, gold for 3 things) in the same PR. **Guide** `docs/GUIDE.md` (daily loop, reading a card, 30-minute walkthrough) in PR #3. Workflow guide for the whole setup: `~/DEV/WORKFLOW.md` + visual https://claude.ai/artifact/9kc2jSrPeGCWzyPAQDpcPt. Handoff: `docs/handoffs/2026-10-03-pm-system-build.md`.\n- 2026-10-03 (late): **Handoff follow-through (Windows).** `mods-sync.ps1` run: 10 mods loaded, 0 invalid (restart pending). `~/.codex/config.toml` model `gpt-6.1-sol` -> `gpt-6-sol` (gpt-6-sol and gpt-6-astra both answered a probe). claude-skills, dotclaude, KeystoneOS and DEV root all match origin. The CATES \"leftover\" worktree is draft PR #1 in CATES, not debris; left for Eric.\n- 2026-10-04: **Board has a stable URL** so it can be a Mac Dock app (Safari → File → Add to Dock). Port 7474 by default (falls back to a free port if taken; `--port 0` = random). Token made once per machine and kept in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\pm-board\\token` / `~/.config/pm-board/token` (`PM_BOARD_TOKEN` overrides). On Windows the server no longer sets SO_REUSEADDR, which let a second server silently share a taken port. 3 new tests in `TestSingleInstance`. Full suite: 305 passed, 7 CLI-subprocess failures (WinError 6), the same 7 as maste