{"parentUuid":"9b0222bb-ec3b-4c96-8fca-80a469271bd9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"29694039-5529-4b2d-92d5-4fa6d92712d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\nDecisions waiting on you — 37 open in 16 repos (STATUS touched in the last 3 days)\n\n2026-10-04  Education_Alignment_Initiative\n    - Deck 39 (social media and mental health) shows \"In an emergency, call 911 · 988 Suicide & Crisis Lifeline\". Keep it, and what is Baylor Athletics' own referral path to add?\n    - The EAI docs mention a 45-topic 5 Slides pipeline, but only 40 topics are written down. Are there five more topics, and where are they?\n\n2026-10-04  NCAA_BestPractices_Doc\n    - Chris, decision 1: best-practice guide or formal department policy? Recommended: guide plus procedures and forms, with a one-page policy statement if he wants one (leadership on 7/30 preferred flexible guidance).\n    - Chris, decision 2: is this document the Software & Technology framework's \"Version 1\" content, or a separate document? Recommended: Version 1. The framework keeps the request and review process (SSI Rec 4).\n    - Chris, decision 3: scope is the four SSI areas only, or the four plus a short education section? Recommended: four plus education (SSI Rec 2 says consent depends on it).\n    - Chris: who owns and signs the document? UT uses its Chief Medical Officer.\n    - Chris: data ownership. Institution-owned with athlete access (the March draft), or athlete-owned for physiologic data (the framework spec)?\n    - Chris: who are the contacts in OGC, Procurement and ITS, and did the May outside-counsel proposal go anywhere?\n    - Chris: is a standing working group with student-athlete members chartered, and can the Rec 2 education ride on existing compliance and orientation sessions?\n    - After the meeting, OGC / Compliance: consent model (blanket or per-instance, notice only or notice plus consent, re-consent cadence), and how HIPAA, FERPA and Texas law classify physiologic versus performance data.\n    - After the meeting, OGC / Procurement: vendor contract terms. Is there a standard data addendum, who audits the roughly 50 contracts, are data-for-discount and norm pooling allowed, what are the exit and deletion duties?\n    - After the meeting, ITS / Compliance: on staff departure, who owns vendor admin accounts and who revokes access; also retention periods and the transfer-athlete protocol.\n    - Eric: DEXA data (DexaProject) sits on a Google Drive attached to a non-Baylor account, but guide §4.2 makes restricted Baylor-controlled storage the rule, and the guide's DEXA row now says \"unverified\". Move it to Baylor…\n    - Eric: three private repos hold identifiable athlete data: diagnostics files in `Ath_Medicine`, athlete JSON in `Catapult_API`'s git history, and a report naming athletes in `S2_Evaluation/docs/program/executive-report.md…\n\n2026-10-04  project-triage\n    - Spelling of \"Laurel Proulx\" (WomensHealth_Survey) not found in any file — confirm with Eric.\n\n2026-10-03  CATES\n    - The white paper's financial figures (350-500% ROI, per-miss and medical cost numbers) have no source attached. Verify or label them as illustrative before they go in front of anyone.\n\n2026-10-03  KeystoneOS\n    - GPS: Eric turns off the GPS step in Windows `Refresh_All_Data` (the Mac now owns the DB). Three old GPS copies still to delete by hand (paths in `docs/audits/2026-09-13-gps-locations.md`).\n    - Backup manifest still routes to OneDrive `Backups/DEV-NonRepo`; OneDrive is dropped.\n\n2026-10-03  Flint\n    - Interview (when Eric has time): `docs/interview-prep.md`, 27 questions. New: slide U4 L1 p.16 (Evans) has \"no more than 4x per year\" body-composition testing, which may be the origin of the same rule in `method-baseline.…\n    - Evans Verkhoshansky activation-levels entry: the slides contradict themselves on where the threshold of adaptability sits; both are recorded and the entry stays `untested` (the course ceiling) rather than `contested`. Er…\n    - Two-a-day entry (Issurin): confirm the current NCAA Division I preseason practice rule before using it for fall camp.\n\n2026-10-03  PlayerProfiles_FB_03-28-2026\n    - Is the 2025-09-01 to 2026-03-28 window still the right reporting range for the 2026 season, or should it roll forward?\n\n2026-10-03  Football/MatchupAnalysis_FB2026\n    - What `(M)`, `(B)`, `(O)` mean in `missed_tackle_detail`. Inference only right now.\n    - Whether PFF charts `all_blocking` for FBS-vs-FCS games at all. Week 3 is FBS-vs-FBS and settles it: if 31257 populates within two days and 31122 still has not, stop promising assignment-level analysis for FCS games.\n\n2026-10-02  S2_Evaluation\n    - Can the flagging threshold be calibrated against anything external, or does the approach need replacing? ADR 0013 leaves this open.\n\n2026-10-02  RTP_Constraints_Course\n    - Linemen's GPS peaks look understated. Does Joe want a timed flying 10–20 yd for OL before using their bands?\n    - Does Joe have Google Drive for Desktop? If not, each new lesson is a re-download.\n\n2026-10-02  RTP_ProgressReport\n    - Are all three report styles still wanted, or has one won?\n\n2026-10-02  42Analytics\n    - Approve or change the proposed Jev bars. Do tier B later?\n    - 5 no-captions videos (incl. `2RJ-6mW_UOM` Ivy League concussion rule): Whisper/other route, or skip?\n    - Cloud-scheduled caption fetch: try one captions-only run first; YouTube often blocks cloud IPs.\n\n2026-10-02  PythonScripts_2024\n    - Does anything here overlap with a live repo (Jump_Dash, BodyWeightWebApp, Catapult_API) closely enough to be worth folding in?\n\nls: /Users/kristinarash/DEV_archive_hold: No such file or directory","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UUW6Vh4inZqGVmaBKmLVYc"}]},"uuid":"4077ea5b-89b1-4e9e-9830-f601e0bf4f27","timestamp":"2026-10-05T12:50:35.240Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\nDecisions waiting on you — 37 open in 16 repo