{"parentUuid":"cfa85b46-91c9-445b-9a92-3b51260f12bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfj92GgopC3gJ7SssEywH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Stack doctor ran.** Your handoff is healthy. Both machines are in sync. The backup, memsearch, flush pipeline and venv all pass.\n\nIt found 5 issues. None of them stops your work today.\n\n1. **`dailybackup` shows exit code 1.** This is old. It is from last night's failed run. The run I did this morning passed. The code resets after tonight's 21:00 run. No action.\n2. **`recall-coverage`:** the memsearch index list includes `~/.codex/memories`. That folder has never existed on this Mac. The fix is to remove line 15 of `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/data/memory-index-paths.json`. It is noise only.\n3. **`errors-log`:** these are the same 3 lines as before. The 2 backup lines are fixed now. The budget trip is still open.\n4. **`USER.md` at 99%** (1356 of 1375 characters). The next memory save to it will force a trim.\n5. **`MEMORY.md` at 99%** (2467 of 2500 characters). Same problem.\n\nOn 10-03 you set a rule: system work waits for the Friday Harness slot, unless it blocks real work. Today is Monday.\n\n**Pick one:**\n1. **Defer all of it to Friday 10-09** (my pick). Nothing here stops your work. The one risk: a memory save before Friday will make me trim USER.md or MEMORY.md on the spot. If that happens, I will ask you first.\n2. **Clear the error log now, defer the rest.** This takes one minute and ends the warning at the start of each session. The two 99% files still wait for Friday.\n\nThen you can choose a repo to work on."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1120,"cache_read_input_tokens":113490,"output_tokens":600,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":51},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","ca