{"parentUuid":"4cb104db-26c6-4871-8390-00d0713a2437","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfjADv8zyoFw3QJz26AnU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S6VPuBaDoJVaA1LLevvoZV","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage/docs/GUIDE.md","old_string":"through git.\n\n## Where to look next","new_string":"through git.\n\nOn Windows: type `pm` in PowerShell. In Edge, open the board, then click **⋯ → Apps →\nInstall this site as an app**. In Chrome, click **⋮ → Cast, save, and share → Install page\nas app**. Tick \"Pin to taskbar\" when asked. Install from the page that has `?token=` in\nthe address bar; the app reopens at that address.\n\nThe icon is the Front Burner ring (`assets/icon-*.png`, drawn by Codex). A Dock app made\nbefore 2026-10-05 has the old icon: remove it from the Dock and add it again.\n\n## Where to look next"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":141589,"output_tokens":1084,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1084,"cache_read_input_tokens":141589,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01S6VPuBaDoJVaA1LLevvoZV":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage/docs/GUIDE.md","old_string":"through git.\n\n## Where to look next","new_string":"through git.\n\nOn Windows: type `pm` in PowerShell. In Edge, open the board, then click **⋯ → Apps →\nInstall this site as an app**. In Chrome, click **⋮ → Cast, save, and share → Install page\nas app**. Tick \"Pin to taskbar\" when asked. Install from the page that has `?token=` in\nthe address bar; the app reopens at that address.\n\nThe icon is the Front Burner ring (`assets/icon-*.png`, drawn by Codex). A Dock app made\nbefore 2026-10-05 has the old icon: remove it from the Dock and add it again.\n\n## Where to look next"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfjADuhhrMrTZ6f4j7jyi","attributionSkill":"codex-build","type":"assistant","uuid":"b1fbf195-838e-4672-b315-4411d85a5c1a","timestamp":"2026-10-05T13:21:22.637Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"67004755-6eb9-4324-a41f-97820a746f73","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"67004755-6eb9-4324-a41f-97820a746f73","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b1fbf195-838e-4672-b315-4411d85a5c1a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"866a6510-800f-4a1f-b4d4-ada25aed5f29","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S6VPuBaDoJVaA1LLevvoZV","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage/docs/GUIDE.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"973e9aa6-8085-441b-b3c0-13a0b5d4870e","timestamp":"2026-10-05T13:21:22.787Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage/docs/GUIDE.md","oldString":"through git.\n\n## Where to look next","newString":"through git.\n\nOn Windows: type `pm` in PowerShell. In Edge, open the board, then click **⋯ → Apps →\nInstall this site as an app**. In Chrome, click **⋮ → Cast, save, and share → Install page\nas app**. Tick \"Pin to taskbar\" when asked. Install from the page that has `?token=` in\nthe address bar; the app reopens at that address.\n\nThe icon is the Front Burner ring (`assets/icon-*.png`, drawn by Codex). A Dock app made\nbefore 2026-10-05 has the old icon: remove it from the Dock and add it again.\n\n## Where to look next","originalFile":"# Using the project board — a working guide\n\nFor Eric. What the README lists, this shows in use. Read top to bottom once\n(about 10 minutes), then do **\"Your first 30 minutes\"** at the end with real projects.\n\n## The idea in four lines\n\n- **The registry** (`portfolio.json`) is the one list of projects. Status, lane, stage,\n  receiver, rank live there.\n- **Each repo's `docs/STATUS.md`** holds the work itself: what happened (dated lines) and\n  what's next. The board reads it and never writes it.\n- **The board** is the front door: one card per project, live, editable.\n- **Three rituals keep it true**: dev-sync opens it, closeout fixes the cards, the Friday\n  review sweeps the paused pile.\n\nThe whole system exists so that six weeks from now you can look at a card and pick a\nproject back up without re-reading the repo.\n\n## Your day with it\n\n**Start.** `dev-sync` (or `/startup`) pulls everything and opens the board. If you skip\nthat, type `pm` in PowerShell or `/pm` in Claude Code. It reuses the board if one is\nalready running, so typing it again is harmless.\n\n**During.** Keep the board open beside the terminal. Work happens in the terminal and the\nrepos; the board catches up within ~3 seconds of any change to the registry or a visible\nproject's STATUS.md. You don't refresh it. Use the board for the things it is good at:\n\n| You want to… | On the board | Or in the terminal |\n|---|---|---|\n| See what's live | Focus view (default) | `portfolio.py slate-check` |\n| Find anything | Search box (every lane, every status) | — |\n| Pick a project up | Open card → **Start** | `portfolio.py set-status X active` |\n| Put one down | Open card → **Park** | `portfolio.py set-status X paused` |\n| Finish one | Open card → **Done** | `portfolio.py set-status X done` |\n| Say who it's for | Open card → receiver field | `portfolio.py set-receiver X \"Kenny Boyd\"` |\n| Re-prioritise | Drag within a column | — |\n| Move a stage | Drag to another column | `portfolio.py set-stage X building` |\n| Log a note | Open card → add update, Enter | `portfolio.py add-update X \"note\"` |\n| Capture an idea | — | `portfolio.py add-idea \"pitch\"` or \"new idea: …\" to Claude |\n\n**End.** Run `closeout`. It checks the card of every project you touched today, fixes the\ngaps with you (below), commits board edits as `data: board edits <date>`, pushes, and\nprints the cards last. Those printed cards are what the other machine, or you next month,\npicks up from.\n\n**Friday.** `weekly-review` now has a sweep: up to 10 paused projects that nobody has\ntouched for 30+ days, oldest first. For each you say **revive** (needs a next step and a\nreceiver), **keep** (parked; it leaves the sweep for 90 days) or **archive**. Anything you\nskip comes back next week. 85 are waiting as of 2026-10-03, so about 8 Fridays clears it.\n\n## Reading a card\n\n```\n 2  NCAA_BestPractices_Doc                    ← rank in the lane · name\n    NCAA best practices document (Chris…)     ← what it is (registry purpose)\n    for      Chris Ruf                        ← receiver\n    stands   08-04 Confirmed as a separate…   ← newest dated line in STATUS (or registry)\n    next     Collect source material and…     ← first item under STATUS ## Next\n    touched  yesterday                        ← last file change, either machine\n    ▪▪▫▫▫▫ idea 1/6               [paused]    ← stage · status\n    7-day rule: 5 days left · needs step 1 done\n    ⚠ Needs a receiver\n```\n\n- **\"nothing on record\"** on `stands` or `next` means the STATUS file is thin. That's the\n  most common reason a card reads badly, and the fix is in the repo, not the board.\n- **\"touched\"** comes from the landed ledger (30 days). Older means \"not in the last month\".\n- **Flags** are the only red on the page. They mean an active project is missing a next\n  step or a receiver.\n- **Hover** the `next` line to see whether it came from STATUS or from the registry, and\n  the `touched` line for the exact time and machine.\n\n## What makes cards good (the part that's on you)\n\nThe board is only as good as STATUS.md. Two habits do almost all of it:\n\n1. **A dated line for each session's progress**, under `## Done` or `## Current state`:\n   ```\n   - 2026-10-03: Week 5 EPA profile built; ASU game-day sheet sent to coaches.\n   ```\n   The card shows the newest one. A registry note dated today does *not* count for\n   closeout; STATUS is the record.\n2. **One concrete first item under `## Next`.** A command to run or a file to open, not a\n   theme. \"Run `pff_game_result.py --week 6` after PFF grades post\" beats \"keep going on\n   matchups\". Strike an item through (`~~done~~`) and the card skips to the next one.\n\n## The rules that push back (on purpose)\n\n- **Slate cap: 5 active job projects.** Start a sixth and the board refuses and says\n  which five are active. Park one first. Other lanes are not capped.\n- **7-day rule.** Starting a job, side or tool project starts a clock. Within 7 days it\n  needs a receiver *and* step 1 done, or the next sync pauses it. The card counts down.\n  Re-start it when there's something to show; the clock restarts.\n- **Receivers.** Job, side and tool projects name who the output is for: a person, or\n  `me: <why>` (a bare \"me\" is refused). system and knowledge projects are exempt.\n- **Focus view hides things.** It shows active projects, paused ones touched in the last\n  14 days, and anything with a charter date in the next 14 days. Each column says how many\n  it hides. Click **Focus** to switch to **All rows**; the choice is remembered.\n\n## Two machines\n\nThe registry travels by git. dev-sync pulls before the board starts; closeout commits and\npushes board edits. The header says **\"N unpushed registry edits\"** while there are any.\nIf you edit on Windows and skip closeout, then edit on the Mac, expect a JSON merge\nconflict: run closeout before switching machines.\n\n## When something's off\n\n- **`pm` says the board did not start:** the log path is in the message. Usually a bad\n  `portfolio.json` (it refuses to start on one; `portfolio.py slate-check` shows the error).\n- **A change in the terminal didn't show up:** is the project in the current view (Focus,\n  lane tab, search)? Polling only watches the STATUS files of cards on screen.\n- **The unpushed-edits count is stale after a push:** it updates on the next registry\n  change. Harmless.\n- **Undo says \"registry changed outside the board\":** something else wrote the file since\n  your last board edit. Undo refuses rather than wipe that change.\n\n## Your first 30 minutes\n\nDo these with real projects; each one teaches one part.\n\n1. **Open it.** New PowerShell → `pm`. (After a Claude Code restart, `/pm` works too.)\n2. **Focus vs All.** Note the job lane's card count, click **Focus** → **All rows**, look at\n   the difference, switch back.\n3. **Search.** Type `cfb` — the lane tabs show where the hits are.\n4. **Fix a real gap.** Weekly_Matchups_2026 is active with \"⚠ Needs a receiver\". Open it,\n   type a receiver (`me: in-season scouting I run`, or a coach's name), click away. The\n   flag disappears.\n5. **Watch it live.** In the terminal, add a dated line to\n   `~/Desktop/DEV/Weekly_Matchups_2026/docs/STATUS.md` (or any visible project's), save,\n   and watch its `stands` line change within a few seconds.\n6. **Feel the cap.** Start a paused job project. (5 slots, 1 used, so it works.) Then Park\n   it again.\n7. **Preview tonight.** `python portfolio.py card-check` — the list closeout will walk you\n   through: today's touched projects and their gaps.\n8. **Preview Friday.** `python portfolio.py sweep` — the first 10 paused projects up for a\n   decision. Look before Friday; you may already know the answers.\n\n## As a Mac app\n\nThe board keeps the same address (port 7474, same token) every time it starts, so it\ncan live in the Dock. On the Mac: run `pm`, then in Safari choose **File → Add to Dock**.\nThe Dock icon opens the board in its own window. It still needs the board running, so\ntype `pm` first (or once a day). On the phone, use Claude (claude.ai/code on the\n`project-triage` repo) with the same `portfolio.py` commands; changes reach the board\nthrough git.\n\n## Where to look next\n\n- `README.md` — full CLI list and what the board can change.\n- `docs/project-management-system-design.md` — why each rule exists, and what was rejected.\n- `COMMANDS.md` (DEV root) — the desk reference across all projects.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":146,"oldLines":6,"newStart":146,"newLines":14,"lines":[" `project-triage` repo) with the same `portfolio.py` commands; changes reach the board"," through git."," ","+On Windows: type `pm` in PowerShell. In Edge, open the board, then click **⋯ → Apps →","+Install this site as an app**. In Chrome, click **⋮ → Cast, save, and share → Install page","+as app**. Tick \"Pin to taskbar\" when asked. Install from the page that has `?token=` in","+the address bar; the app reopens at that address.","+","+The icon is the Front Burner ring (`assets/icon-*.png`, drawn by Codex). A Dock app made","+before 2026-10-05 has the old icon: remove it from the Dock and add it again.","+"," ## Where to look next"," "," - `README.md` — full CLI list and what the board can change."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b1fbf195-838e-4672-b315-4411d85a5c1a","session_id":"67004755-6eb9-4324-a41f-97820a746f73","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"67004755-6eb9-4324-a41f-97820a746f73","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"973e9aa6-8085-441b-b3c0-13a0b5d4870e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfjADv8zyoFw3QJz26AnU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FKM5qhvjfMn7cf6uqtqGvc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/DEV/project-triage && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/STATUS.md'; s=open(p).read()\nline=\"- 2026-10-05 (Mac): **App icon.** Codex drew 3 concepts (`assets/icon-candidates/`); A (gold burner ring with cards) is served as `/icon-{32,180,192,512}.png` plus `/manifest.webmanifest` (no `start_url`, so the installed app keeps `?token=`). Tab title is now \\\"Front Burner\\\". Installable from Edge/Chrome on Windows (steps in GUIDE \\\"As a Mac app\\\"). Suite: 312 ran, 2 crosswalk `TestNestedRepos` failures that also fail on the code before this change.\\n\"\ns=s.replace(\"\\n## Next\\n\", \"\\n\"+line+\"\\n## Next\\n\",1) if \"\\n\\n## Next\\n\" not in s else s.replace(\"\\n\\n## Next\\n\",\"\\n\"+line+\"\\n## Next\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"## Next\\n\",\"## Next\\n- **Windows:** `git pull` here, `pm`, then install the board as an app from Edge (GUIDE \\\"As a Mac app\\\").\\n- Fix the 2 failing crosswalk tests (`tests/test_crosswalk.py` `TestNestedRepos`); they fail on master too.\\n\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nT=$'\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jh4bFo8QkgSAL2Ng4RJ9sz'\ngit add docs/GUIDE.md docs/STATUS.md && git commit -qm \"docs: Windows install steps; STATUS for app icon$T\" && git push -q 2>&1|tail -1; git status -sb|head -1; sed -n '/^## Next/,+3p' docs/STATUS.md","description":"Update STATUS, commit and push docs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":141589,"output_tokens":1084,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server