{"parentUuid":"c5e64ed5-2419-4b90-8413-c7ee4a500bf3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"ELI5"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f364dbd4-99a5-43ec-a120-d41ebe004ffa","timestamp":"2026-10-05T13:21:36.699Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nELI5 output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"67004755-6eb9-4324-a41f-97820a746f73","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"67004755-6eb9-4324-a41f-97820a746f73","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f364dbd4-99a5-43ec-a120-d41ebe004ffa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfjAFDsdM8PkdUMS2d6g6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The board has a new icon now, and it can be installed as an app on both machines.\n\n**The icon:** Codex drew 3 ideas. I picked **A**: a gold burner ring with project cards on it, on Baylor green. It fits the board's name, \"Front Burner\". I dropped C because it looked like a poop emoji. All 3 are in `~/DEV/project-triage/assets/icon-candidates/` if you want a different one.\n\n- The board now shows this icon on the browser tab and on an installed app. The tab title is now \"Front Burner\".\n- The board's own tests pass. 2 other tests fail (in `tests/test_crosswalk.py`), but they failed before my change too. I added them to the to-do list in STATUS.\n- I restarted the board. The new icon is live. Everything is committed and pushed.\n\n**Your Mac Dock app still has the old icon.** To fix it:\n1. Right-click the Dock icon → **Options → Remove from Dock**.\n2. In Safari, open `http://127.0.0.1:7474/?token=3aFtektgzqjcy7Xn0TGPlg`\n3. Click **File → Add to Dock**.\n\n**On Windows:**\n1. In PowerShell, go to the project-triage folder and run `git pull`.\n2. Type `pm`. The board opens in your browser.\n3. In Edge: **⋯ → Apps → Install this site as an app**. In Chrome: **⋮ → Cast, save, and share → Install page as app**.\n4. Tick **Pin to taskbar**.\n\nInstall from the page whose address ends in `?token=...`. If not, the app opens without your token and shows no data. These steps are also in `docs/GUIDE.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":143506,"output_tokens":558,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ep